      "result": {
        "kind": "question",
        "status": "partial",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Under the manual, alcohol or drug influence is not a reason to exclude an accident from the CIDE/ASCIDE conventions. So the fact that Car B’s driver was found under the influence does not, by itself, prevent their application. The manual also says that, for CIDE, the authority’s involvement is irrelevant and only the front of the D.A.A. is valid.",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "sha256:b9c70c74911fad7992a01f77d861a33f10f8313c96a9f58c09b2f448a54c8344:page:9",
              "sha256:b9c70c74911fad7992a01f77d861a33f10f8313c96a9f58c09b2f448a54c8344:page:10",
              "sha256:b9c70c74911fad7992a01f77d861a33f10f8313c96a9f58c09b2f448a54c8344:page:11"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "However, the conventions apply only to material damage to the vehicles themselves. Car A’s driver’s bodily injuries—including serious injuries—must be dealt with outside the conventions. The supplied text does not establish whether the convention applies to this particular accident overall; it does not provide the facts needed to assess all eligibility conditions or the applicable accident documentation. This describes the November 2004 manual, not current law.",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "sha256:b9c70c74911fad7992a01f77d861a33f10f8313c96a9f58c09b2f448a54c8344:page:26",
              "sha256:b9c70c74911fad7992a01f77d861a33f10f8313c96a9f58c09b2f448a54c8344:page:27",
              "sha256:b9c70c74911fad7992a01f77d861a33f10f8313c96a9f58c09b2f448a54c8344:page:28"
            ]
